<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nemesis (1839)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nemesis was an iron-hulled paddle steamer built by John Laird at Birkenhead in 1839 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, the first ocean-going iron warship. With a shallow draught and heavy guns, she served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a> from 1840, destroying Chinese war junks and leading British forces up rivers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Canton</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>, showing the power of steam warships against Qing defences.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nemesis-1839.jpg" alt="Nemesis (1839)" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: S. Bull (engraver) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HEIC_Nemesis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
